cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use VASPBERRY 1.6.5, cite this source version,
  the exact commit, and the scientific method references appropriate to
  the calculation you performed.
title: VASPBERRY
type: software
version: 1.6.5
date-released: '2026-10-04'
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Hyun-Jung
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5602-1404"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Infant83/VASPBERRY"
url: "https://github.com/Infant83/VASPBERRY"
abstract: >-
  VASPBERRY uses standard VASP WAVEDER optical matrices for supported Kubo charge
  response and WAVECAR wavefunctions for geometric and explicitly selected
  approximate calculations of Berry curvature,
  Chern numbers, projected-spin Chern sectors and Kubo curvature,
  a Fukui-Hatsugai n-field Z2 invariant, circular dichroism,
  and circular optical selection. General matrix post-processing provides
  versioned point-curvature data, two-dimensional intrinsic charge Hall
  transport, conventional insulating spin Hall response, and VASP-derived
  Wannier interpolation with full-connection charge Hall integration.
